// R11 row 5, CLOSED 2026-09-15: reassigning an `arc` `var` leaked the
// previous box. `emitAssign` now evaluates the new value into a temporary,
// drops the old box, then stores, so every iteration's `v = "two"` releases
// the box from the previous one. Measured 0 on both witnesses; it read 3000
// on both before, and the gate went red on the old pin before the constant
// moved. Scoped to `arc` vars: an `owned` var may be aliased by a list
// element that never marks it moved, so `owned` reassignment stays R16's
// revival leak.
//
// Status: parses, passes `cell check`. LLVM and MLIR refuse it (arc is
// scalar-first-refused there, same as examples/arc.cell). Lives under
// examples/leaks/ so it is invisible to the top-level corpus loops (see
// examples/leaks/README.md).

pub fn print_int(copy value: Int);

pub fn main() {
    var arc v = "one"
    var i = 0
    while i < 1000 {
        v = "two"
        i = i + 1
    }
    print_int(i)
}
